  "title": "Janie N Probable NDE 6198",
  "date": "2/12/12",
  "content": "I have a low tolerance for medication but I have chronic insomnia. I take Ambien to sleep every night. Yesterday, I took Ambien and another drug to sleep. I recall passing out at 8:30 at night. I recall, in the middle of the night, having problems breathing and feeling my heart beat slow down. I was unable to get up, although I was not sleeping. The next thing I recall was floating from the ground into the air. The sky was very blue. It was completely silent and my body did not feel any flow of air around me or feel like I was projected forward in any way. I was simply floating towards the sky. I recall the feeling that I could travel anywhere and see anything. I looked around me. I saw the sky and what appeared to be castles and green valleys. I felt light, and comfortable. There continued to be no sound and there was no sense of warmth or cold; just complete comfort. At one point, I knew that I could keep going and there was no anxiety in that idea. I recall turning around at some point and not seeing the ground any longer. As I was floating upwards, my body simply turned around and started to go back. It was not a choice I made, nor did I have a feeling that I had to go back. I simply went back. I opened my eyes in bed and noticed that my body was extremely cold and that my heartbeat was extremely slow. I have been taking Ambien for 4 years and I have never had an experience like this before. It was unlike a dream in many ways, and I don't believe it was a dream.",
